 "method_limits": [
  "the population is E507's own published face; a pair appears here because that face called it ambiguous, not because this study re-read the upstream rows",
  "the scoped table resolves a name to the nearest enclosing scope that binds it, then the module; it is not a dataflow analysis, so a name rebound later in the same scope still contributes every assignment to that scope",
  "comprehension targets are shadowed (E507 already did this) and a lambda body is treated as its own scope",
  "a symbol that the enclosing scope does not bind and that is a parameter of the enclosing function is published as caller-supplied, never folded into clock/data",
  "the resolver cache is keyed without the table in key, so it is cleared per arm; a shared cache would answer one table with the other table's result",
  "only the tree is read: the git-history arm of E507 is not replayed here, so a pair whose only binding was historical is out of this study's reach"
